<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Clemens August of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1700–1761</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Clemens August of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> was a Wittelsbach prince who gathered church offices on a grand scale, becoming Archbishop-Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a> from 1723, Prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> of Münster, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paderborn">Paderborn</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hildesheim">Hildesheim</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osnabruck">Osnabrück</a>, and Grand Master of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>. He thus ruled a large part of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duchy-of-westphalia">Duchy of Westphalia</a>. He spent lavishly on rococo palaces, among them Augustusburg at Brühl, and on hunting.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/clemens-august-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="Clemens August of Bavaria" width="320" height="431" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georg Desmarées · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clemens_August_of_Bavaria_as_Grand_Master_of_Teutonic_Knights.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
